  "notes": "バテる may come from \"batter\" (as in exhausting oneself through repeated effort) or from {果|は}てる (to reach the end/be exhausted). It's particularly associated with summer heat exhaustion ({夏|なつ}バテ).\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is a casual/colloquial verb. In formal contexts, use {疲労|ひろう}する or {疲|つか}れ{切|き}る.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {夏|なつ}バテ: summer fatigue/heat exhaustion\n- バテ{気味|ぎみ}: feeling somewhat exhausted\n- バテている: to be in an exhausted state\n\nASPECT (ている):\nバテている indicates an ongoing state of exhaustion.",
